-- Evolve only the untouched starting brief; preserve owner edits and saved ideas.
UPDATE design_entries SET content=json_set(content,'$.text','Explore the whole courtyard behind the pool with an eating area, a lounge with two daybeds and cozy seats in every layout. Keep the existing L-shaped arrangement, including the long slightly angled west wing, the shallow north loggia, and its uncovered front terrace. Retain the roof, posts, existing outdoor fireplace, timber character, tree and pool. Compare three source-based isometric studies: A, a generous banquette table at the north terrace with west-wing daybeds and fireside chairs; B, two north-bay daybeds with a round outdoor dining table in front and cozy fireside chairs; C, a compact dining nook and separate sofa in the north bay, plus west-wing daybeds and fireside chairs. Use natural timber furniture, soft oatmeal and sage fabrics and restrained stone details. Keep routes to the house, adjoining rooms and pool practical. The isometric illustrations omit the existing roof only to reveal the arrangement; this is not a roof-removal or pergola proposal. The source-plan outline governs the layout. Furniture, tree position, glazed opening details and heights remain indicative; verify door swings, chair pull-out space, rain coverage and fit with a survey. Earlier concepts remain available in the archive.'),version=version+1,updated_at=strftime('%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%fZ','now') WHERE project='courtyard' AND kind='brief' AND json_extract(content,'$.text')='Reimagine the covered patio in the courtyard behind the pool. This is an open exploration: compare a restful lounge, a dining and entertaining space, and a flexible combination. Preserve the character of the timber-clad buildings and use natural materials. Initially retain the existing roof and structural posts; any larger structural changes require separate feasibility work. Improve comfort, furniture layout, lighting and connection to the pool. Seek inspiration before fixing the programme. Compare three layouts across the whole L: A, a fireplace lounge with dining in the perpendicular bay; B, dining beside the fireplace with a separate pool-facing lounge; C, a garden salon with several smaller seating areas and a daybed, leaving formal dining to the east terrace. Keep circulation between the house, pool and both covered bays clear. The newer photographs reveal an existing outdoor fireplace and the full L-shaped courtyard. Retain that fireplace as a design anchor unless a later study explicitly proposes otherwise.';
